// What the player reads for each of the game's names: "BirchBark" is "birch bark", "Hypothermia" (an
// effect) is "hypothermic". Lower case; the words that use them capitalise a sentence's start (Names.Cap).
// One row for every value of each enum listed here, no more (Names.Tables): a value added in code
// without its words fails at load. Gear and recipes are named in items.json and recipes.json.
// EffectKind reads after "You are" ("You are shivering", "You are in pain").
// Requirement reads after "needs" ("needs a fire burning"). Capability names the tool by what it does
// ("the cutting tool"). The fight's own names (actions, range, a fighter's state) join when the
// combat round's rework settles them.
